/target
**/*.rs.bk

# The lock file is committed on purpose. An unpinned dependency tree would let a
# conformance verdict change without a commit, which is the drift this project
# exists to make visible.
Cargo.lock.orig

# Contract fixtures are compiled from the sources beside them during
# integration tests. The artefacts are reproducible and are not committed.
fixtures/contracts/target

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store

# A developer's own network credentials are never tracked. The documented form
# for local configuration is `estamora.local.toml`.
estamora.local.toml
*.local.toml
.env
.env.*

# Insta snapshots are reviewed and committed; the pending directory is not.
**/*.snap.new
**/.insta-pending

# The Soroban test host writes a JSON snapshot of ledger state beside the tests
# that use it. It is host state, not an artefact of this repository: two hosts at
# the same ledger point produce it, its contents are an SDK implementation
# detail, and committing it would make an SDK upgrade look like a change to the
# runner.
test_snapshots/
